{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2094 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "fc4bd0374bc033af39ee1e809ad019c9fd593e050c6d2fb229517144a1fa458c" :edb/db-before-t 2093 :edb/db-after-t 2094 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535406 50 #inst "2026-10-08T23:30:58.541Z" 13194139535406 true] [17592186048981 1007 #edb/ref 17592186347592 13194139535406 true] [17592186128959 1100 "Find the volume of the solid $R$, given by\n$R = \\Big\\{(x,y,z) \\:: \\: 1 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\: 0 \\leq z \\leq \\sqrt{2y}, \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq yz \\Big\\}$." 13194139535406 false] [17592186128959 1100 "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR = \\Big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: 1 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\: 0 \\leq z \\leq \\sqrt{2y}, \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq yz \\Big\\}.\n$$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186128959 1145 "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type II region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nV &= ∭_(R)dV \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{2y}}∫_{0}^{yz}dxdzdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{2y}}[x]_{x = 0}^{x = yz}dzdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{2y}}yzdzdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}y[\\frac{z^{2}}{2}]_{z = 0}^{z = \\sqrt{2y}}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}\\frac{y}{2}(\\sqrt{2y})^{2}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}y^{2}dy \\\\\n&= [\\frac{y^{3}}{3}]_{y = 1}^{y = 2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}(8 - 1) - 0 \\\\\n&= \\frac{7}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535406 false] [17592186128959 1145 "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type II region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2y}}{\\int }_{0}^{yz}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2y}}[x]_{x=0}^{x=yz}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2y}}yz\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y{[\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=\\sqrt{2y}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{y}{2}{(\\sqrt{2y})}^{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(8-1)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186128960 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/043adf0ef683c24fbf4680145411d86fa94b52016bee44ac8f08ca7c5ca9f1b7.png)\n\n \n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" 13194139535406 true] [17592186128960 1100 "Find the volume of the solid region above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2053/Source/Images/833b93599de9c6b708f3a1261e746f92.png)\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" 13194139535406 false] [17592186128960 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/75a76a2dbc34c889335e66623e12b686eb9a255ee0d67f9be0e3792f2650360c.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type I region\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: (x,y) \\in D, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 4-x-y \\big\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 2 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/e19ffe6a0555851c2b05526272beb21dbcdc082a23a2e11809c661666efdf133.png)\n\nHence, the type I representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 4-x-y \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-x-y}dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=4-x-y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(4-x-y)-0\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4-x-y\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[(4-x)y-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}((4-x)(2)-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2})-0\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6-2x\\,dx \\\\  & =[6x-{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(6(1)-{1}^{2})-0 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186128960 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2053/Source/Images/2298616a278bfc40c45434c5731feaf7.png)\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type I region\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{(x,y,z) \\:: \\: (x,y) \\in D, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 4-x-y \\big\\}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 2 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2053/Source/Images/cc9d4db3f6570233d1e1e71d8636bcdc.png)\n\nHence, the type I representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{(x,y,z) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 4-x-y \\big\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nV &= ∭_(R)dV \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}∫_{0}^{4 - x - y}dzdydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}[z]_{z = 0}^{z = 4 - x - y}dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}(4 - x - y) - 0dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}4 - x - ydydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}[(4 - x)y - \\frac{y^{2}}{2}]_{y = 0}^{y = 2}dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}((4 - x)(2) - \\frac{2^{2}}{2}) - 0dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}6 - 2xdx \\\\\n&= [6x - x^{2}]_{x = 0}^{x = 1} \\\\\n&= (6(1) - 1^{2}) - 0 \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535406 false] [17592186128961 1100 "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the surface ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/9597cda64435e7e578c996c4c5d3e3056705e5c4fb79ccbb9bbf48cd7befe296.png) the plane ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/cd3b605899fbd8e49350a7f9fc6184911d4308e39ec94fe5b072cf0697b131f8.png) and the planes ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/7eb560050bef519d15d7bea27856044c51d6bdd794b40b95f2dd8a3c50e59c0f.png) ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/ffebc693860930a5435af764f3707689c9f70fc4ad6c764dfac1a124e65356c1.png) ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/565885d259d0dbf65c2faa6f43d18dcfba04ca1249bda3e90d0c2f433e80a8b4.png) ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/76bc9b4689fb88451fa5003bc31ef3c12d7dbcbae6955da504fbce27d0345829.png)" 13194139535406 true] [17592186128961 1100 "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the surface $y=xz$, the plane $y=2$, and the planes $x=0$, $x=1$, $z=0$, $z=1$." 13194139535406 false] [17592186128961 1145 "Notice that our solid can be written as a type III region.\n\nFor each point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/2a3a167677bfdfb8d87dff88867664d5f458ead614c4ec27b43bb2e498bde545.png) in the rectangular base region\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/341b60cfc6c2a2005ddf74477e9cb5a3daa5f9c64194ecef6c65c4df0295dbf4.png)\nthe variable ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/523ba398cc130edb20b50aa7b9a5deab0a53e4222824e3deda7f1a13ac7b0a56.png) runs from the surface\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/a0569d8f914ef9ad9e121ee79be25a1decce6381aedf54e3eb5ef633f652fe8e.png)\nup to the plane\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/0f1adb561fc36d233b9c2711b7da31566c8e9475b3ac442677963c5fdf54e5ac.png)\n\nSo we can write:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/f2c48bb89e04bcbf32e367ed0cdf260f7fa0630b3039f0fd842bfd418a5b124e.png)\n\nTherefore, the volume of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/f49bc07ef2d4d420878a9a9a3fab238aa47bed7fb96828ab0249cfd0c7419484.png) is given by the following triple integral:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/37f11eb812a19788af700184269ef20eb4cef4115fef59477afb49da067d940f.png)" 13194139535406 true] [17592186128961 1145 "Notice that our solid can be written as a type III region:\n\n$$\nR = \\left\\{(x,y,z) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 1, \\:\\: xz \\leq y \\leq 2 \\right\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nV &= ∭_(R)dV \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{1}∫_{xz}^{2}dydzdx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{1}[y]_{y = xz}^{y = 2}dzdx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{1}2 - xzdzdx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}[2z - \\frac{xz^{2}}{2}]_{z = 0}^{z = 1}dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}[2(1 - 0) - (x(1^{2} - 0))/(2)]dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}2 - \\frac{x}{2}dx \\\\\n&= [2x - \\frac{x^{2}}{4}]_{x = 0}^{x = 1} \\\\\n&= (2 - \\frac{1}{4}) - 0 \\\\\n&= \\frac{7}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535406 false] [17592186129140 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347593 13194139535406 true] [17592186129140 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347600 13194139535406 true] [17592186129140 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347607 13194139535406 true] [17592186129140 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347614 13194139535406 true] [17592186129141 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347656 13194139535406 true] [17592186129141 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347663 13194139535406 true] [17592186129141 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347705 13194139535406 true] [17592186129141 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347712 13194139535406 true] [17592186129142 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347621 13194139535406 true] [17592186129142 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347628 13194139535406 true] [17592186129142 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347635 13194139535406 true] [17592186129142 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347642 13194139535406 true] [17592186129142 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347649 13194139535406 true] [17592186129701 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535406 true] [17592186129701 1100 "Find the volume of the solid $R$, given by\n\n$R = {(x, y, z): - 2 \\le y \\le 0, 0 \\le z \\le 2 + y, 1 \\le x \\le y - z + 3}$." 13194139535406 false] [17592186129701 1100 "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-2\\le y\\le 0,\\,0\\le z\\le 2+y,\\,1\\le x\\le y-z+3}.\n$$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186129701 1145 "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type II region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{2+y}{\\int }_{1}^{y-z+3}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{2+y}[x]_{x=1}^{x=y-z+3}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{2+y}(y-z+3)-1\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{2+y}y-z+2\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{[(y+2)z-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=2+y}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}((y+2)(2+y)-\\frac{(2+y)^{2}}{2})-0\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{y}^{2}+4y+4\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}+2{y}^{2}+4y]}_{y=-2}^{y=0} \\\\  & =0-\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{(-2)^{3}}{3}+2(-2)^{2}+4(-2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186129702 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535406 true] [17592186129702 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/7456b549ac815ab491945d9b3f2873d65b091636f7b8282f296a435954ba503d.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the right one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" 13194139535406 true] [17592186129702 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2053/Source/Images/q-40353.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the right one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" 13194139535406 false] [17592186129702 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/702e54d6f4b951eec56a62d340f81df1f618622114cfef6045460a6d184bffbc.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-x-z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/af505b53a12bbe74da4d3885df59c4c00cc7bfaf71df9f7167caa9dbf67cfb73.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-x-z}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3-x-z}dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[y]_{y=0}^{y=3-x-z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(3-x-z)-0\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}3-x-z\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[(3-x)z-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}((3-x)(1)-\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2})-0\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5}{2}-x\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{5}{2}x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{5}{2}(1)-\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2})-0 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347591 1089 "e-26133" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347591 1100 "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloids ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/9145bfbf3c349359595396d06807191dc666c03558e5943e18d6a356d3b52e80.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/98d18317cb2e69f489be66c8a4244e90327ed05aa0de5633fb6c461d81936a89.png) whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/7ebb2715de5217f0bd211be342bd8b64026a641254d79e7dde54606c712f0af3.png)\n\nFind ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/cd9dbda80a5f41e2eba8b5440f42eddc12015a003e558ea26fd512cf1827a7a3.png) ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/54827258e24002d07ac1bc4468c8a8f81fa9ee932f102790093989c200860788.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/1b0eaf7c23571a3806b1fdbcb5badeb8127cefe1f5d71ea8d1ea426aa2e0fbff.png)" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347591 1113 #uuid "7ff9ca14-f66e-5921-b3c0-15961feb071a" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347591 1145 "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/3397de904d08c80f853cc9ad930c0792c5f6033aa1409655c4623fe3a0edfc86.png)-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/de82f740c53922156a55045b891d73187af742855d8687380f2147468b6625a4.png)\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/b7058c5c6e450acdb37c5e67a76139fe8c17abcc4003b200af69d62540050db9.png)-plane is a circle.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type III region:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/081a487a9615ca41e08647729d379a07b4c63e856d8db5d20357ee6e379f9e56.png)\nwhere ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/5990121d9274012f291f6d3622d0ba077bd009023969faa36b1058d05f4e1962.png) is the interior of the circle ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/eab35e9389dfcc153b3ff22e36ff359595c386b3733d61589a04807c25bc56cf.png)\n\nAs a result, the volume of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/e72f4ff500bcbe3f2392425e3b4b777888f579ae6ece9546ca0dae0c08c33493.png) is given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/2d850bd7a9cc12a8143f7ee1a9803e4d6ea98ae1c22cfc56e1c5ce989b512f94.png)\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/837e84cb3633847bb8928cfb823f7c20756bd92362517e5411a0e77684da47a8.png) consists of\n\n- the lower part ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/5e020d44aa4de1a4a3c561677f7b0a46ffc9a6b5f1a670fdb4d6ec93f837bf15.png) and\n\n- the upper part ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/674107266131d1e4e7e3b7147c7eab59e380cbb30c04c44f8942b0ea688973ac.png)\n\nfor ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/542abe7b3c7cdba70586108ad546acee635ad90d16326b8bad3f7ba430de3f08.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/3c8cf015e3b1944ce18fa83f77a17912afc696e485dc6557760a1d78bfd81e3c.png)\n\nSo,\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/1bc658f161ad3523eaf0a263af0a9b86cb596483fe0f20f6088af1f366ff205f.png)" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347592 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347670 13194139535406 true] [17592186347592 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347677 13194139535406 true] [17592186347592 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347684 13194139535406 true] [17592186347592 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347691 13194139535406 true] [17592186347592 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347698 13194139535406 true] [17592186347592 1049 "Finding a Double-Integral Formula for Volume" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347592 1105 #edb/ref 17592186347591 13194139535406 true] [17592186347592 1119 #uuid "13f9ed67-24d8-5d41-8f82-1296abc57f12" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347593 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347594 13194139535406 true] [17592186347593 1089 "q-161653" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347593 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535406 true] [17592186347593 1100 "Find the volume of the solid $R$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,2\\le z\\le 3y+x}.\n$$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347593 1113 #uuid "72d6f8d0-1f35-5a19-b558-bcfd9f34f6df" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347593 1145 "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type I region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{2}^{3y+x}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}[z]_{z=2}^{z=3y+x}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}3y+x-2\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+xy-2y]}_{y=1}^{y=4}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,[(24+4x-8)-(\\frac{3}{2}+x-2)]\\,dx \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{2}3x+\\frac{33}{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{33}{2}x]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{33}{2}(2)-0 \\\\  & =39.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347595 13194139535406 true] [17592186347594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347596 13194139535406 true] [17592186347594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347597 13194139535406 true] [17592186347594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347598 13194139535406 true] [17592186347594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347599 13194139535406 true] [17592186347594 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535406 true] [17592186347594 1041 "selection" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347594 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347597 13194139535406 true] [17592186347594 1110 #uuid "635a1867-36b4-5b88-bb71-5e9e1ee7e72a" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347595 1034 "\\frac{32}{3}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347595 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347595 1111 #uuid "e59ffa58-74f1-562a-a741-d4c6351b9270" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347596 1034 "27" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347596 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347596 1111 #uuid "ebeb9cd6-3829-5945-8ab6-7f8f8cf7d489" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347597 1034 "39" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347597 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347597 1111 #uuid "2b3d4c71-66a0-5a85-ac89-57300619ce15" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347598 1034 "24" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347598 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347598 1111 #uuid "6bb1709d-cb10-583f-9d82-bf25a8b48b20" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347599 1034 "\\frac{33}{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347599 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347599 1111 #uuid "f9433e48-13ab-58b9-a220-8fc15935944c" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347600 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347601 13194139535406 true] [17592186347600 1089 "q-161656" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347600 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535406 true] [17592186347600 1100 "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,0\\le z\\le 2y,\\,0\\le x\\le y+2z}.\n$$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347600 1113 #uuid "f08aba5b-443f-57e6-8701-3029a49c21a4" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347600 1145 "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type II region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}{\\int }_{0}^{y+2z}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}[x]_{x=0}^{x=y+2z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}y+2z\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{[yz+{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=2y}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}y(2y)+(2y)^{2}-0\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}6{y}^{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={[2{y}^{3}]}_{y=1}^{y=3} \\\\  & =2(3)^{3}-2(1)^{3}-0 \\\\  & =52.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347602 13194139535406 true] [17592186347601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347603 13194139535406 true] [17592186347601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347604 13194139535406 true] [17592186347601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347605 13194139535406 true] [17592186347601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347606 13194139535406 true] [17592186347601 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535406 true] [17592186347601 1041 "selection" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347601 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347604 13194139535406 true] [17592186347601 1110 #uuid "25be8db5-531d-50bf-8e2c-d021aadd0e64" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347602 1034 "\\frac{27}{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347602 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347602 1111 #uuid "037237d7-c28f-54f5-adf4-134ac6f4b141" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347603 1034 "\\frac{53}{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347603 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347603 1111 #uuid "cc462843-fb53-56a5-b557-a644bae05960" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347604 1034 "52" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347604 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347604 1111 #uuid "19500e0b-841c-58fc-b770-14aa998983e1" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347605 1034 "56" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347605 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347605 1111 #uuid "a7e25b2b-eaa7-52e7-bab7-47cd2dcb5fc5" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347606 1034 "23" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347606 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347606 1111 #uuid "29506a0f-81c2-577d-8660-457520696835" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347607 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347608 13194139535406 true] [17592186347607 1089 "q-161657" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347607 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535406 true] [17592186347607 1100 "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,1\\le z\\le 3,\\,0\\le x\\le 2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}.\n$$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347607 1113 #uuid "685f5c88-d6f7-5d95-bc6d-097dd6fed3b8" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347607 1145 "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type II region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}[x]_{x=0}^{x=2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,{[{z}^{2}]}_{z=1}^{z=3}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y({3}^{2}-{1}^{2})\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}8\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,dy \\\\  & =8[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y]_{y=0}^{y=\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-8(0-1) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347609 13194139535406 true] [17592186347608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347610 13194139535406 true] [17592186347608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347611 13194139535406 true] [17592186347608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347612 13194139535406 true] [17592186347608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347613 13194139535406 true] [17592186347608 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535406 true] [17592186347608 1041 "selection" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347608 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347611 13194139535406 true] [17592186347608 1110 #uuid "2e6dd80f-da63-5cab-8de9-ae7ccd48407d" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347609 1034 "\\frac{7}{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347609 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347609 1111 #uuid "1024fdbc-83bd-5faf-ba5d-5093ca5c9caf" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347610 1034 "\\frac{9}{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347610 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347610 1111 #uuid "a3c5a6ce-cc61-545a-bbd2-dcbc68b1d804" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347611 1034 "8" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347611 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347611 1111 #uuid "f3be178f-5390-5a71-99a0-d0ceb47603fa" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347612 1034 "2" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347612 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347612 1111 #uuid "14a411e9-4c25-59ea-865b-12c23e2a14b1" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347613 1034 "4" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347613 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347613 1111 #uuid "eb663a61-1e86-5bfd-abf9-45e475d7d7ae" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347614 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347615 13194139535406 true] [17592186347614 1089 "q-161659" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347614 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535406 true] [17592186347614 1100 "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le \\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}},\\,0\\le y\\le 2z}.\n$$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347614 1113 #uuid "9ab8e166-680c-5883-9f97-66afbfcc44a9" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347614 1145 "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type III region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}{\\int }_{0}^{2z}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}[y]_{y=0}^{y=2z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}2z\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{[{z}^{2}]}_{z=-0}^{z=\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{(\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}})}^{2}-0\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}2-{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[2x-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{x=-2}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(2(2)-\\frac{1}{3}(2)^{3})-(2(-2)-\\frac{1}{3}(-2)^{3}) \\\\  & =(4-\\frac{8}{3})-(-4+\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347616 13194139535406 true] [17592186347615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347617 13194139535406 true] [17592186347615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347618 13194139535406 true] [17592186347615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347619 13194139535406 true] [17592186347615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347620 13194139535406 true] [17592186347615 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535406 true] [17592186347615 1041 "selection" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347615 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347619 13194139535406 true] [17592186347615 1110 #uuid "9d3ca650-3e2b-5b33-bd49-57b9bd062470" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347616 1034 "\\frac{9}{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347616 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347616 1111 #uuid "903a36b0-2df4-5939-b9bd-0873e6e07dcc" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347617 1034 "3" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347617 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347617 1111 #uuid "cb041ec0-9c6c-5ad5-9495-7ff8c30ef3f5" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347618 1034 "8" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347618 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347618 1111 #uuid "ecdb8e8e-1ead-5c2f-8d11-87110257f63d" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347619 1034 "\\frac{8}{3}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347619 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347619 1111 #uuid "a87a5d93-f289-5dda-942b-2017705bfade" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347620 1034 "4" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347620 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347620 1111 #uuid "aed7bd19-f8b0-597d-b737-419d7e9b3deb" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347621 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347622 13194139535406 true] [17592186347621 1089 "q-161677" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347621 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535406 true] [17592186347621 1100 "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the $xy$-plane, the surface $z=4-{x}^{2},$ and the planes $x=0,$ $x=2,$ $y=0,$ $y=2.$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347621 1113 #uuid "00e947c4-55c5-5d76-b7c7-7a54f4ff0b9b" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347621 1145 "Notice that our solid can be written as a type I region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 4-{x}^{2}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-{x}^{2}}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=4-{x}^{2}}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4-{x}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(4-{x}^{2})[y]_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(4-{x}^{2})(2-0)\\,dx \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{2}4-{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & =2{[4x-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =2(4(2)-\\frac{1}{3}({2}^{3}))-0 \\\\  & =2(\\frac{16}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347623 13194139535406 true] [17592186347622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347624 13194139535406 true] [17592186347622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347625 13194139535406 true] [17592186347622 1000 #