0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/74954715928551ebb271cdfd461d783778b02b7944cbfd5502d6d06011408ad8.png)\n\nHence, the type I representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3+x-y}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3+x-y}dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=3+x-y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3+x-y)-0\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3+x-y\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[(3+x)y-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}((3+x)(2)-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2})-0\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}4+2x\\,dx \\\\  & =[4x+{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(8+4)-0 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347658 13194139535406 true] [17592186347657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347659 13194139535406 true] [17592186347657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347660 13194139535406 true] [17592186347657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347661 13194139535406 true] [17592186347657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347662 13194139535406 true] [17592186347657 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535406 true] [17592186347657 1041 "selection" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347657 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347658 13194139535406 true] [17592186347657 1110 #uuid "fa94fe5f-46af-5496-bf12-970fee73f52b" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347658 1034 "12" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347658 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347658 1111 #uuid "1a793928-bb3c-5eaa-8721-72e91886cc9f" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347659 1034 "10" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347659 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347659 1111 #uuid "52021203-ee29-52ae-8cbb-cd4367b1d17f" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347660 1034 "16" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347660 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347660 1111 #uuid "c658fb48-b655-5636-a827-9793a38a4b83" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347661 1034 "14" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347661 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347661 1111 #uuid "34016ea3-c3e9-5cd2-af9e-af92072bad4c" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347662 1034 "18" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347662 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347662 1111 #uuid "52a932a2-f5e5-5f78-b875-a9181035b1ec" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347663 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347664 13194139535406 true] [17592186347663 1089 "q-161699" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347663 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535406 true] [17592186347663 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/237856bbfdfa6c5ecaead68d257270bb86aeca666fe4170be50b88b67d3ab9de.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the right one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347663 1113 #uuid "3725fa5e-4286-5db6-99d1-eca169a9fe12" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347663 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/33d937ccc1ae72f5add46a9358af4427147205a072ca2848a44d61288e705235.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1+\\frac{x}{2}+z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/9e7c6fad45d9d85bad5ca16a2000e4d44a1739ab70797e41ae94945a4ffb02ef.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1+\\frac{x}{2}+z}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1+x/2+z}dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[y]_{y=0}^{y=1+x/2+z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(1+\\frac{x}{2}+z)-0\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}1+\\frac{x}{2}+z\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[(1+\\frac{x}{2})z+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}((1+\\frac{x}{2})(2)+\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2})-0\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}4+x\\,dx \\\\  & ={[4x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(8+2)-0 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347664 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347665 13194139535406 true] [17592186347664 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347666 13194139535406 true] [17592186347664 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347667 13194139535406 true] [17592186347664 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347668 13194139535406 true] [17592186347664 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347669 13194139535406 true] [17592186347664 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535406 true] [17592186347664 1041 "selection" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347664 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347666 13194139535406 true] [17592186347664 1110 #uuid "4da7669f-6b58-58bc-a92e-3bb1cc0dd734" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347665 1034 "12" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347665 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347665 1111 #uuid "7d6bca99-70ea-561b-b5e4-446adda9a23f" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347666 1034 "10" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347666 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347666 1111 #uuid "a1e56578-1ef1-5752-83e9-a32e45a82dc0" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347667 1034 "8" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347667 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347667 1111 #uuid "4686037a-3fba-5a25-86e1-efcfe0588e32" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347668 1034 "14" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347668 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347668 1111 #uuid "a77239a8-9197-50b0-a4b1-60eeee73a73c" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347669 1034 "6" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347669 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347669 1111 #uuid "f09dd3d1-791b-5fee-b31f-d003ca12b419" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347670 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347671 13194139535406 true] [17592186347670 1089 "q-161705" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347670 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535406 true] [17592186347670 1100 "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloids $z=-3+6{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}$ and $z=-1+5{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2}}^{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{a(x)}^{b(x)}\\,f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347670 1113 #uuid "89397d8f-ca3d-5aa6-936a-51ec58a30523" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347670 1145 "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $xy$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3+6{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2} & =-1+5{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+2{y}^{2} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $xy$-plane is an ellipse.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type I region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,-3+6{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}\\le z\\le -1+5{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the ellipse ${x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}=2.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-3+6{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}}^{-1+5{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}}\\text{d}z]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-1+5{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2})-(-3+6{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2-{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of\n\n- the lower part $y=-\\sqrt{1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $y=\\sqrt{1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}},$\n\nfor $-\\sqrt{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2-{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2}}^{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/2}}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/2}}\\,2-{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}})}^{2}+(2-{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+(2-{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =4-2{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347671 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347672 13194139535406 true] [17592186347671 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347673 13194139535406 true] [17592186347671 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347674 13194139535406 true] [17592186347671 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347675 13194139535406 true] [17592186347671 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347676 13194139535406 true] [17592186347671 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535406 true] [17592186347671 1041 "selection" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347671 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347672 13194139535406 true] [17592186347671 1110 #uuid "48730a7d-deb3-50d2-89fc-c90c617250f3" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347672 1034 "4-2{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347672 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347672 1111 #uuid "f59903f9-90a6-5fef-bb48-3b229090796d" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347673 1034 "3+{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347673 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347673 1111 #uuid "7f937aa2-2f71-51e0-9e5c-59231ef9464e" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347674 1034 "6-5{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347674 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347674 1111 #uuid "d2f1b6bf-1da5-569e-9f17-9116a6d6ba69" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347675 1034 "3+2{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347675 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347675 1111 #uuid "612a1ef7-161e-5596-b387-3809377e8e86" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347676 1034 "6-3{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347676 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347676 1111 #uuid "45a92263-7e80-56ae-8d27-f1ee9fc79b67" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347677 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347678 13194139535406 true] [17592186347677 1089 "q-161706" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347677 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535406 true] [17592186347677 1100 "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloid $x=3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2}$ and the parabolic cylinder $x=1-{y}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}{\\int }_{a(y)}^{b(y)}\\,f(y,z)\\,dz\\,dy\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347677 1113 #uuid "cc058cbe-e1e2-5f16-ac7c-3f82322fc472" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347677 1145 "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $yz$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2} & =1-{y}^{2} \\\\ 4{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $yz$-plane is a circle.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type II region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2}\\le x\\le 1-{y}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the circle ${y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}^{1-{y}^{2}}\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(1-{y}^{2})-(3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}1-4{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $z=-\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{1-4{y}^{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $z=\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{1-4{y}^{2}},$\n\nfor $-\\frac{1}{2}\\le y\\le \\frac{1}{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}1-4{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{1-4{y}^{2}}/2}^{\\sqrt{1-4{y}^{2}}/2}\\,1-4{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{1-4{y}^{2}})}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{1-4{y}^{2}})}^{2}+(1-4{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(1-4{y}^{2})+\\frac{1}{4}(1-4{y}^{2})+(1-4{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}-6{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347678 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347679 13194139535406 true] [17592186347678 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347680 13194139535406 true] [17592186347678 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347681 13194139535406 true] [17592186347678 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347682 13194139535406 true] [17592186347678 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347683 13194139535406 true] [17592186347678 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535406 true] [17592186347678 1041 "selection" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347678 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347682 13194139535406 true] [17592186347678 1110 #uuid "ebec8cdf-063c-518e-9a10-f0c9c2def370" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347679 1034 "1-6{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347679 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347679 1111 #uuid "f145ccfb-cf24-5fab-b67d-8c29becde622" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347680 1034 "3-9{y}^{2}-8{z}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347680 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347680 1111 #uuid "30d1acc5-d4db-5f45-b854-0d5990517f11" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347681 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{9}{2}{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347681 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347681 1111 #uuid "6e4b795a-adfc-536c-a041-03b3545126a5" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347682 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}-6{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347682 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347682 1111 #uuid "6d953ce0-5168-5182-a5bc-591fb6c34ebe" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347683 1034 "3+6{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347683 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347683 1111 #uuid "356d94d6-0bd1-5e41-9097-40ce9acb653c" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347684 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347685 13194139535406 true] [17592186347684 1089 "q-161715" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347684 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535406 true] [17592186347684 1100 "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloid $x=-2+{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2}$ and the parabolic cylinder $x=-1+2{z}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{a(y)}^{b(y)}\\,f(y,z)\\,dz\\,dy\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347684 1113 #uuid "0e6b7281-889f-50e9-9a22-290c6faa279a" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347684 1145 "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $yz$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2+{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2} & =-1+2{z}^{2} \\\\ {y}^{2}+2{z}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {y}^{2}+2{z}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $yz$-plane is an ellipse.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type II region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,-2+{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2}\\le x\\le -1+2{z}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the ellipse ${y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}=1.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-2+{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}^{-1+2{z}^{2}}\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-1+2{z}^{2})-(-2+{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}1-{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $z=-\\sqrt{\\frac{1-{y}^{2}}{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $z=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-{y}^{2}}{2}},$\n\nfor $-1\\le y\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}1-{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{(1-{y}^{2})/2}}^{\\sqrt{(1-{y}^{2})/2}}\\,1-{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{\\frac{1-{y}^{2}}{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{\\frac{1-{y}^{2}}{2}})}^{2}+(1-{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{1-{y}^{2}}{2}+(1-{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =2-2{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347685 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347686 13194139535406 true] [17592186347685 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347687 13194139535406 true] [17592186347685 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347688 13194139535406 true] [17592186347685 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347689 13194139535406 true] [17592186347685 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347690 13194139535406 true] [17592186347685 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535406 true] [17592186347685 1041 "selection" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347685 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347688 13194139535406 true] [17592186347685 1110 #uuid "75ddea3b-8b6e-5f00-bba3-7ddfc6866b6e" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347686 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}-2{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347686 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347686 1111 #uuid "bed9cc6a-c49f-54bc-ae2a-57b717f707c3" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347687 1034 "1-3{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347687 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347687 1111 #uuid "7aa00230-1a42-52e6-b198-b25b620298c4" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347688 1034 "2-2{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347688 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347688 1111 #uuid "6f097bee-f125-586a-b709-6d8b508194da" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347689 1034 "3+6{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347689 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347689 1111 #uuid "f78d6104-4d38-5693-aa16-b2a6c273c53a" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347690 1034 "2-{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347690 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347690 1111 #uuid "8223a7de-6c9a-5f4b-b9a8-c06dd97f1542" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347691 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347692 13194139535406 true] [17592186347691 1089 "q-161716" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347691 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535406 true] [17592186347691 1100 "Consider the solid enclosed between the parabolic cylinders $y=4{x}^{2}$ and $y=1-2{z}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}{\\int }_{a(x)}^{b(x)}\\,f(x,z)\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347691 1113 #uuid "82f158da-cdbf-547c-a9f3-2ae44cc23680" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347691 1145 "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $xz$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2} & =1-2{z}^{2} \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+2{z}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $xz$-plane is an ellipse.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type III region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 1-2{z}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the elipse $4{x}^{2}+2{z}^{2}=1.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{4{x}^{2}}^{1-2{z}^{2}}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(1-2{z}^{2})-(4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}1-2{z}^{2}-4{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $z=-\\sqrt{\\frac{1-4{x}^{2}}{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $z=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-4{x}^{2}}{2}},$\n\nfor $-\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}1-2{z}^{2}-4{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{(1-4{x}^{2})/2}}^{\\sqrt{(1-4{x}^{2})/2}}\\,1-2{z}^{2}-4{x}^{2}\\,dz\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{\\frac{1-4{x}^{2}}{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{\\frac{1-4{x}^{2}}{2}})}^{2}+(1-2{z}^{2}-4{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1-4{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{1-4{x}^{2}}{2}+(1-2{z}^{2}-4{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =2-8{x}^{2}-2{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347692 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347693 13194139535406 true] [17592186347692 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347694 13194139535406 true] [17592186347692 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347695 13194139535406 true] [17592186347692 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347696 13194139535406 true] [17592186347692 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347697 13194139535406 true] [17592186347692 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535406 true] [17592186347692 1041 "selection" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347692 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347696 13194139535406 true] [17592186347692 1110 #uuid "59b74bed-7004-5cad-9792-eceb1faaefdd" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347693 1034 "2-{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347693 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347693 1111 #uuid "e2070529-2d39-522b-a99e-d62f4510a384" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347694 1034 "1-4{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347694 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347694 1111 #uuid "b273525f-901c-52ab-9559-ada9ca874695" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347695 1034 "1+3{x}^{2}-2{z}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347695 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347695 1111 #uuid "a7181fb2-19fc-5bca-bb2a-a442347734f1" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347696 1034 "2-8{x}^{2}-2{z}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347696 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347696 1111 #uuid "e2a1214b-5c29-5a5f-843a-c1bb30b7e11f" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347697 1034 "1-6{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347697 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347697 1111 #uuid "69e58e3c-0755-5025-9ac4-11db537e9348" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347698 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347699 13194139535406 true] [17592186347698 1089 "q-161719" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347698 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535406 true] [17592186347698 1100 "Consider the solid enclosed between the parabolic cylinders $y=-2+3{x}^{2}$ and $y=-4{z}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{6}/3}^{\\sqrt{6}/3}{\\int }_{a(x)}^{b(x)}\\,f(x,z)\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347698 1113 #uuid "38ab4bd5-173d-559d-9de9-30730176f570" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347698 1145 "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $xz$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2+3{x}^{2} & =-4{z}^{2} \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $xz$-plane is an ellipse.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type III region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,-2+3{x}^{2}\\le y\\le -4{z}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the ellipse $3{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}=2.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-2+3{x}^{2}}^{-4{z}^{2}}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-4{z}^{2})-(-2+3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2-3{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $z=-\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{2-3{x}^{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $z=\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{2-3{x}^{2}},$\n\nfor $-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}\\le x\\le \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2-3{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{6}/3}^{\\sqrt{6}/3}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2-3{x}^{2}}/2}^{\\sqrt{2-3{x}^{2}}/2}\\,2-3{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{2-3{x}^{2}})}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{2-3{x}^{2}})}^{2}+(2-3{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2-3{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{2-3{x}^{2}}{4}+(2-3{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =3-\\frac{9}{2}{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347699 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347700 13194139535406 true] [17592186347699 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347701 13194139535406 true] [17592186347699 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347702 13194139535406 true] [17592186347699 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347703 13194139535406 true] [17592186347699 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347704 13194139535406 true] [17592186347699 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535406 true] [17592186347699 1041 "selection" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347699 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347704 13194139535406 true] [17592186347699 1110 #uuid "ccb749c9-311c-5d81-9c66-b181b18805a4" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347700 1034 "1-\\frac{9}{2}{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347700 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347700 1111 #uuid "60dd21e0-6406-5d58-85a0-afe7c6186d10" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347701 1034 "1-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+2{z}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347701 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347701 1111 #uuid "1b79a634-8460-5a18-a62d-b7ca64861db7" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347702 1034 "2+9{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347702 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347702 1111 #uuid "3c92bfe3-1fe8-5653-9109-78a6c1b03032" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347703 1034 "3-9{x}^{2}-2{z}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347703 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347703 1111 #uuid "307a6187-bf40-5c08-b148-f242e734d7a8" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347704 1034 "3-\\frac{9}{2}{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347704 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347704 1111 #uuid "ac9dd0f0-9460-5682-8523-40e0d3d98ca1" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347705 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347706 13194139535406 true] [17592186347705 1089 "q-161739" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347705 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535406 true] [17592186347705 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/4485b56f6b31059b42d379993951d94952397fe01bd1b5922b0ea8e7b171f8f6.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347705 1113 #uuid "5be76099-fab4-5c16-9f1f-54513eb4e9fd" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347705 1145 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/66593acc794ee28d8372ec5758abf14594ea58528c1fe793917754dd9d21c5ad.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type I region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 6-3x-2y},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo find the top boundary curve of $D$ in the form $y=y(x),$ we substitute $z=0$ into the equation $z=6-3x-2y:$\n\n$$\n0=6-3x-2y\\,⟹\\,y=3-\\frac{3}{2}x\n$$\n\nThen, we have\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-\\frac{3}{2}x},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/8b3edbf61dc8a2b2a027c79a0ac1bbee54163b89277040119aaea382121998ff.png)\n\nHence, the type I representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-\\frac{3}{2}x,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 6-3x-2y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3-3x/2}{\\int }_{0}^{6-3x-2y}dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3-3x/2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=6-3x-2y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3-3x/2}(6-3x-2y)-0\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3-3x/2}6-3x-2y\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[(6-3x)y-{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=3-3x/2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}((6-3x)(3-\\frac{3x}{2})-{(3-\\frac{3x}{2})}^{2})-0\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3-\\frac{3x}{2})((6-3x)-(3-\\frac{3x}{2}))\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3-\\frac{3x}{2})(3-\\frac{3x}{2})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{(3-\\frac{3x}{2})}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}9-9x+\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{4}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[9x-\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{3{x}^{3}}{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(9(2)-\\frac{9(2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{3(2)^{3}}{4})-0 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347706 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347707 13194139535406 true] [17592186347706 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347708 13194139535406 true] [17592186347706 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347709 13194139535406 true] [17592186347706 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347710 13194139535406 true] [17592186347706 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347711 13194139535406 true] [17592186347706 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535406 true] [17592186347706 1041 "selection" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347706 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347710 13194139535406 true] [17592186347706 1110 #uuid "82d2a86a-27e9-50f1-a5a2-0c90fa48a49f" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347707 1034 "9" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347707 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347707 1111 #uuid "d1bb0d5e-e280-50ef-8ca8-a2cd73e51a6c" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347708 1034 "8" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347708 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347708 1111 #uuid "3ccb700b-e908-5a96-85c7-3b7220e22b82" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347709 1034 "7" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347709 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535406 true] [17592186347709 1111 #uuid "494dcf07-02d7-5acb-8cd0-d5c4bc681b42" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347710 1034 "6" 13194139535406 true] [17592186347710 1103 #edb/ref 17592